    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://w3id.org/ad4gd/ev/ebv"/>
    <skos:definition>Productivity in an ecosystem refers to the percentage of energy that enters the ecosystem in the form of biomass at a particular trophic level. It is the rate at which biomass is formed in the ecosystem. Net pimary production.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel>Primary productivity of terrestrial biomass production net pimary production</skos:prefLabel>
